# Consent and CSP

## Consent

- Consent Mode v2 uses **region-specific defaults** in `Analytics.astro` (gtag `consent default` + `region`):
  - **EEA / UK (`GB`) / CH:** `ad_storage`, `ad_user_data`, `ad_personalization`, and `analytics_storage` are **denied** until Google’s CMP (or Accept when ads are off) updates them.
  - **Everywhere else:** `analytics_storage` (and ad storage signals) are **granted** by default so GA4 counts users; the site banner offers **Reject / Do not sell or share**, which denies all four and stores `docuforge:cookie-ok=0`.
- EEA / UK / CH: Google AdSense Privacy & messaging (Funding Choices / IAB TCF) is the CMP when ads are on. Worker sets `window.__docuklinGeo` via `consentRegions.ts`; hide the site cookie bar there when ads are enabled.
- Other regions: site Accept + Reject / Do not sell or share banner (opt-out). Do not invent a second CMP stack.
- Load `gtag.js` promptly (no `requestIdleCallback` deferral). Queue custom events through `dataLayer` when the gtag stub is not ready (`src/lib/analytics.ts`).

## CSP (`public/_headers`)

- Keep the allowlist tight. Add hosts only for documented vendor needs + a real console violation.
- Required today: GA4, AdSense + `fundingchoicesmessages.google.com`, Cloudflare Web Analytics, EmailJS (`api.emailjs.com` + jsDelivr SDK). See comments in `_headers` and `AGENTS.md`.
